From: AudioWRT <audiowrt@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] hostap: keep -s compatible with CONFIG_NO_STDOUT_DEBUG

OpenWrt launches both hostapd and wpa_supplicant with -s from /etc/init.d/wpad.
The option is enabled by CONFIG_DEBUG_SYSLOG, but upstream places the syslog
open/close implementations inside !CONFIG_NO_STDOUT_DEBUG.

AudioWRT deliberately removes stdout/debug formatting to save flash. Keep the
standard -s command-line contract while making the syslog setup calls no-ops in
that constrained build instead of pulling the full debug implementation back
in.

--- a/src/utils/wpa_debug.h
+++ b/src/utils/wpa_debug.h
@@ -309,7 +309,8 @@ enum hostapd_logger_level {
 };
 
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_DEBUG_SYSLOG
+#if defined(CONFIG_DEBUG_SYSLOG) && \
+	!defined(CONFIG_NO_STDOUT_DEBUG)
 
 void wpa_debug_open_syslog(void);
 void wpa_debug_close_syslog(void);
